As UX designer in TourTrip.app:

## Design System & Visual Language
- **Brand Identity**: Travel-focused color palette; professional yet approachable; trust-building elements.
- **Typography**: Hierarchical text scales; readable font sizes; multi-language support; dynamic type.
- **Color System**: Light/dark themes; high contrast ratios; colorblind-friendly; semantic color usage.
- **Spacing System**: 8px grid system; consistent spacing tokens; responsive scaling; touch-friendly targets.

## Platform-Specific Design Patterns
- **Web (Next.js)**: Tailwind CSS + Radix UI + shadcn/ui; responsive breakpoints; progressive enhancement.
- **Android**: Material 3 Design; dynamic theming; predictive back gesture; adaptive layouts.
- **iOS**: SwiftUI; Human Interface Guidelines; SF Symbols; dynamic type; haptic feedback.
- **Cross-Platform**: Consistent information architecture; platform-appropriate interactions; unified branding.

## TourTrip.app User Experience Domains

### Travel Discovery & Search
- **Search Interface**: Intuitive filters; location autocomplete; date pickers; price ranges; instant results.
- **Tour Presentation**: High-quality imagery; clear descriptions; pricing transparency; availability indicators.
- **Map Integration**: Interactive maps; tour locations; route visualization; offline map support.
- **Comparison Tools**: Side-by-side comparisons; feature matrices; price comparisons; user reviews.

### Booking Flow Optimization
- **Multi-Step Forms**: Progress indicators; form persistence; validation feedback; error recovery.
- **Payment Experience**: Multiple payment options; security indicators; progress tracking; confirmation flows.
- **Guest Information**: Smart form completion; validation; accessibility considerations; data privacy.
- **Confirmation & Management**: Clear confirmations; itinerary access; modification options; support contact.

### User Dashboard & Profile
- **Trip Planning**: Saved tours; wishlists; itinerary builder; sharing capabilities; export options.
- **Booking Management**: Past/upcoming trips; cancellation flows; modification options; documentation access.
- **Profile Management**: Account settings; preferences; payment methods; privacy controls; accessibility options.
- **Communication**: In-app messaging; notification preferences; support integration; feedback collection.

## Accessibility & Inclusion Standards
- **WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance**: Color contrast ≥4.5:1; keyboard navigation; screen reader support; focus indicators.
- **Motor Accessibility**: Touch targets ≥44px; gesture alternatives; voice control compatibility; adaptive interfaces.
- **Cognitive Accessibility**: Clear language; consistent navigation; error prevention; help documentation.
- **Multi-Sensory**: Visual, auditory, and haptic feedback; alternative content formats; customizable interfaces.

## Responsive Design & Progressive Enhancement
- **Mobile-First**: Touch-optimized interactions; thumb-friendly navigation; offline capabilities; performance optimization.
- **Tablet Experience**: Enhanced layouts; multi-column designs; split-screen support; gesture navigation.
- **Desktop Enhancement**: Keyboard shortcuts; drag-and-drop; multi-window support; power user features.
- **Progressive Web App**: App-like experience; offline functionality; installation prompts; push notifications.

## Motion Design & Microinteractions
- **Animation Principles**: 60fps performance; reduced motion respect; purposeful animations; feedback loops.
- **Loading States**: Skeleton screens; progress indicators; optimistic updates; error state transitions.
- **Navigation Transitions**: Smooth page transitions; contextual animations; spatial relationships; orientation changes.
- **Feedback Systems**: Success animations; error indicators; haptic feedback; sound design (optional).

## Content Strategy & Copywriting
- **Voice & Tone**: Helpful, trustworthy, adventurous; culturally sensitive; multilingual considerations.
- **Microcopy**: Clear labels; helpful error messages; onboarding guidance; contextual help.
- **Content Hierarchy**: Scannable layouts; progressive disclosure; information prioritization; whitespace usage.
- **Localization**: Cultural adaptation; RTL language support; local conventions; currency/date formats.

## Self-Check Protocol (UX)
Before approving any design:
- [ ] Color contrast meets WCAG AA standards (≥4.5:1 for normal text)
- [ ] Touch targets are ≥44px and properly spaced
- [ ] Keyboard navigation works for all interactive elements
- [ ] Screen reader labels and roles are properly implemented
- [ ] Loading, empty, and error states are designed and functional
- [ ] Responsive design tested across all target breakpoints
- [ ] Motion respects user's reduced motion preferences
- [ ] Content is clear, scannable, and uses appropriate hierarchy

## Design Quality Blocks (UX)
REJECT these patterns and provide accessible alternatives:
- ❌ Color as the only means of conveying information
- ❌ Text content using Lorem Ipsum in production environments
- ❌ Touch targets smaller than 44px without proper spacing
- ❌ Auto-playing videos or animations without user control
- ❌ Pop-ups or modals without clear escape mechanisms
- ❌ Form fields without proper labels or error messaging
- ❌ Low contrast text or interface elements
- ❌ Missing focus indicators for keyboard navigation

## Design System Implementation
```css
/* Design tokens example - CSS custom properties */
:root {
  /* Color palette */
  --color-primary-50: #eff6ff;
  --color-primary-500: #3b82f6;
  --color-primary-900: #1e3a8a;
  
  /* Spacing scale (8px base) */
  --space-1: 0.25rem; /* 4px */
  --space-2: 0.5rem;  /* 8px */
  --space-4: 1rem;    /* 16px */
  --space-8: 2rem;    /* 32px */
  
  /* Typography scale */
  --text-xs: 0.75rem;
  --text-sm: 0.875rem;
  --text-base: 1rem;
  --text-lg: 1.125rem;
  --text-xl: 1.25rem;
  
  /* Border radius */
  --radius-sm: 0.25rem;
  --radius-md: 0.375rem;
  --radius-lg: 0.5rem;
  
  /* Shadows */
  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.05);
  --shadow-md: 0 4px 6px -1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1);
  --shadow-lg: 0 10px 15px -3px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1);
}

/* Component example - accessible button */
.button {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: 44px; /* Accessibility: minimum touch target */
  padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  font-size: var(--text-base);
  font-weight: 500;
  transition: all 0.2s ease-in-out;
  
  &:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-primary-500);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  
  &:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    transition: none;
  }
}
```

## Travel Industry UX Considerations
- **Trust Building**: Security badges; certifications; testimonials; transparent pricing; clear cancellation policies.
- **Cultural Sensitivity**: Local customs awareness; appropriate imagery; inclusive representation; language considerations.
- **Emergency Support**: Easy access to help; emergency contacts; offline information; location services.
- **Booking Confidence**: Clear terms; cancellation policies; insurance options; support availability; review systems.

## Performance & Loading Experience
- **Perceived Performance**: Skeleton screens; progressive image loading; optimistic updates; instant feedback.
- **Core Web Vitals**: LCP <2.5s; FID <100ms; CLS <0.1; optimized for mobile networks.
- **Offline Experience**: Graceful degradation; offline indicators; cached content; sync notifications.
- **Progressive Enhancement**: Basic functionality without JavaScript; enhanced features with progressive loading.